    "selected_model": {
      "name": "Probabilistic rainfall-runoff and 2D flood scenario model",
      "why": "It can turn several plausible 2026 storms into runoff, flow routes, water depth and affected-building ranges. A machine-learning forecast alone is not suitable because the project does not yet have enough checked flood-depth observations for training.",
      "current_status": "The map uses the land, drainage and other local evidence to identify places needing closer review. It does not yet predict flood depth or the chance of flooding in 2026.",
      "implementation": [
        "Build low, central and severe 2026 storm scenarios from official forecasts and historical rainfall.",
        "Convert rainfall to runoff using land cover, soil and drainage condition.",
        "Route runoff through a checked surface and drainage model.",
        "Report a range of water depths and affected buildings, including uncertainty."
      ],
      "preferred_tools": "SWMM for drains linked to HEC-RAS 2D or LISFLOOD-FP for surface flow, after drainage levels and structures are checked."
